# pdxdig -- caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md).
#
# `!KIND_FOO <mask>` = mandatory: exec fails -EACCES if the parent's
# cap-set does not hold at least this mask. ` KIND_FOO <mask>` (no
# `!`) = optional: narrowed to at most this mask, dropped to zero if
# the parent held none.
#
# pdxdig's role: DNS query CLI, `dig`-equivalent (paideia-os design/
# networking/r100-user-tools-plan.md §6). At v1.3 the real UDP query
# path is still BLOCKED on §12.1 (kernel-side SOCK_DGRAM extension,
# R100-PREP-002) -- src/dig_query.pdx (pdxdig#4) documents the real
# `net_resolve` extern contract but calls nothing outside this repo
# yet. The tool body exercises the argv surface (including a REAL
# --server= IPv4 parse, pdxdig#5), the response walker (CNAME follow,
# RCODE parse), the semantic-pipe emit wire, and a libpdx-audit STUB
# wire (pdxdig#7, src/audit_wire.pdx) end to end.
#
# Kind rationale:
#   KIND_USER          -- invoker attribution (audit record identity);
#                         every satellite in the R100 wave lists this.
#   KIND_UDP_SOCKET    -- optional at v1.1 (real body is stubbed pending
#                         §12.1 -- sendto/recvfrom sysnos 96/97 not yet
#                         wired to a user-visible surface). Kept in
#                         the decl so the query path can be flipped
#                         from stub-to-real by src/*.pdx edits alone
#                         at pdxdig M2-001 without a caps.decl churn.
#   KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT  -- optional; documentation-only at v1.1.
#                         sys_semantic_send (SC+ ID 115) takes NO cap
#                         slot -- schema is opaque to the kernel and
#                         the producer is capability-ungated at
#                         R107-M0-001. The entry is retained so a
#                         future KIND_SEMANTIC_PIPE recv-side cap
#                         (arriving with the consumer wave) has a
#                         stable spot to land without a caps.decl
#                         churn.

!KIND_USER               0x001   # invoker attribution (audit)
 KIND_UDP_SOCKET         0x00B   # optional -- v1.1 stub; M2-001 real
 KIND_TCP_SOCKET         0x00B   # optional -- Wave mu-03 (pdxdig#8): REAL
                                 # sys_socket/sys_connect/sys_send/sys_recv
                                 # to <resolver>:853 on --dot=1 (src/dot_wire.pdx)
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT       0x001   # optional -- documentation-only
